WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.317 --> 00:00:01.352
- Good morning believe nation,

00:00:01.352 --> 00:00:05.827
today's message is, get up,
over to you, Bill Clinton.

00:00:05.827 --> 00:00:08.283
(rooster crows)

00:00:08.283 --> 00:00:10.821
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:10.821 --> 00:00:13.507
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:13.507 --> 00:00:17.570
♫ I wake every morning

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:21.320
- If whatever it is
doesn't work out, get up.

00:00:23.848 --> 00:00:25.574
I lost two elections, I was the youngest

00:00:25.574 --> 00:00:27.328
former governor in American History.

00:00:27.328 --> 00:00:28.755
(audience laughs)

00:00:28.755 --> 00:00:29.818
After the Reagan landslide,

00:00:29.818 --> 00:00:32.016
I had one guy appointed to the cabinet,

00:00:32.016 --> 00:00:34.545
walk across Main St. in Little Rock,

00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:37.010
to avoid being seen shaking hands with me

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.633
for fear that the guy that
beat me would fire him.

00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:43.897
That was a humbling experience.

00:00:43.897 --> 00:00:47.173
And I think you got to realize,

00:00:47.173 --> 00:00:50.390
there's no personal ambition you have,

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.890
which can be extinguished by anybody else.

00:00:55.706 --> 00:00:59.873
Only you, by giving up your
dreams, can extinguish them.

00:01:02.779 --> 00:01:06.607
And if it doesn't work out
exactly like you intended,

00:01:06.607 --> 00:01:08.338
it'll still take you
someplace interesting,

00:01:08.338 --> 00:01:09.683
and you'll make a difference.

00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:12.433
So my advice is what George said,

00:01:13.752 --> 00:01:16.416
don't be afraid to fail,
but you probably will

00:01:16.416 --> 00:01:18.702
whether you're afraid to or not.

00:01:18.702 --> 00:01:21.869
And it's scary, you just got to get up.

00:01:22.978 --> 00:01:26.864
The world belongs to
tomorrow, not yesterday.

00:01:26.864 --> 00:01:30.294
Don't give anybody else
permission to take your life away.

00:01:30.294 --> 00:01:32.632
Just keep living and keep giving,

00:01:32.632 --> 00:01:34.800
and never make the perfect enemy to good.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.187
Never think that what I'm doing

00:01:37.187 --> 00:01:38.861
is too little to make a difference.

00:01:38.861 --> 00:01:41.611
That's not true, that's not true.

00:01:43.906 --> 00:01:46.511
Do something every day.

00:01:46.511 --> 00:01:50.389
Someday, for all of us,
it'll be our last day.

00:01:50.389 --> 00:01:51.998
And what will matter were all the steps

00:01:51.998 --> 00:01:55.387
we took along the way,
and what they amounted to.

00:01:55.387 --> 00:01:58.137
Not the home run we hit on day x.

00:01:59.258 --> 00:02:02.084
- Your setback is only
a failure if you quit.

00:02:02.084 --> 00:02:05.760
Your setback is only
a failure if you quit.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.409
If you look at the most
successful people in

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:09.811
the world they had tons of setbacks.

00:02:09.811 --> 00:02:12.973
They had setback after setback
after setback after setback.

00:02:12.973 --> 00:02:14.576
And then they started to win.

00:02:14.576 --> 00:02:17.014
And then they had more setbacks
and then they won some more.

00:02:17.014 --> 00:02:17.911
That's part of the journey,

00:02:17.911 --> 00:02:20.114
there's nobody who wakes up, is born,

00:02:20.114 --> 00:02:21.722
and just wins all the time.

00:02:21.722 --> 00:02:23.538
The people who have won the most,

00:02:23.538 --> 00:02:25.693
also had the most setbacks.

00:02:25.693 --> 00:02:28.183
And this is across entrepreneurship,

00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:32.851
athletes, singers, you
always suck at the start.

00:02:32.851 --> 00:02:34.574
You're always going to have setbacks,

00:02:34.574 --> 00:02:36.913
and it's only really a failure if you take

00:02:36.913 --> 00:02:40.440
that setback and don't learn
anything from it, and quit.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.887
If you really want to do something,

00:02:41.887 --> 00:02:45.638
and you try it and you
fail, it didn't work out.

00:02:45.638 --> 00:02:47.292
And then you stop and
say "that wasn't for me,

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:48.434
I'm going to move onto something else".

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.450
If that's your habit,
if that's your cycle,

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.442
it's going to repeat,
because the first time

00:02:52.442 --> 00:02:54.971
we try anything it's not going to work.

00:02:54.971 --> 00:02:56.786
The first you tried
skateboarding or you tried

00:02:56.786 --> 00:02:59.513
to learn a language or you
tried asking a girl out.

00:02:59.513 --> 00:03:03.013
The first time you try anything
is probably not going to work.

00:03:03.013 --> 00:03:04.481
It's not going to be great.

00:03:04.481 --> 00:03:07.277
And the more you do it, the
stronger your muscle builds,

00:03:07.277 --> 00:03:08.696
and the better you get at it.

00:03:08.696 --> 00:03:12.258
And so one of the keys
to success in any field

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:16.294
is constant experimentation,
constant trials,

00:03:16.294 --> 00:03:20.707
constant errors and
constant getting back up.

00:03:20.707 --> 00:03:22.817
If I look at this YouTube
channel as an example,

00:03:22.817 --> 00:03:26.047
we have tried more new
series and failed at them,

00:03:26.047 --> 00:03:29.435
and left them, than most
people have ever launched.

00:03:29.435 --> 00:03:32.853
And we learned from those and
some of them we make better.

00:03:32.853 --> 00:03:34.704
If you look at even our Top 10 series,

00:03:34.704 --> 00:03:36.556
look at the very first one that we did,

00:03:36.556 --> 00:03:38.510
and look at where they're at now.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.583
There's been a lot of improvement.

00:03:40.583 --> 00:03:43.540
The clip quality is better,
the editing is better,

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.964
the transitions are better,
the intros are better,

00:03:45.964 --> 00:03:47.837
the bonuses are better,
everything is better.

00:03:47.837 --> 00:03:49.712
It's gotten better with
more experimentations.

00:03:49.712 --> 00:03:51.449
And not every experiment works.

00:03:51.449 --> 00:03:53.398
And it's been a lot of new
series that we've launched

00:03:53.398 --> 00:03:55.690
that we tried a couple
times and it didn't work,

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:56.896
and so we stopped them and moved on

00:03:56.896 --> 00:03:58.540
to something else, and learn from those.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.978
If you expect the first
time you put something out

00:04:00.978 --> 00:04:02.989
to be amazing, if you
make a YouTube channel,

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:04.702
and you expect your first video to pop,

00:04:04.702 --> 00:04:06.284
you're in for a really rude awakening.

00:04:06.284 --> 00:04:09.101
It's not how the world
works, and that's okay.

00:04:09.101 --> 00:04:13.877
Accept that, get better,
move on, and get back up.

00:04:13.877 --> 00:04:16.073
I'm remembered of the
Thomas Edison about how

00:04:16.073 --> 00:04:19.891
he didn't fail a thousand
times in making a light bulb,

00:04:19.891 --> 00:04:22.778
he just found 999 ways
that it didn't work,

00:04:22.778 --> 00:04:24.180
and then the last one that he did,

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.613
like would you stick with an idea

00:04:25.613 --> 00:04:28.071
a thousand times until you get it to work?

00:04:28.071 --> 00:04:30.488
Like most people, they'll try it once,

00:04:30.488 --> 00:04:32.364
a lot of people once and they're out.

00:04:32.364 --> 00:04:33.633
A lot of people don't even try,

00:04:33.633 --> 00:04:35.764
a lot of people just have
the thought in their head

00:04:35.764 --> 00:04:38.276
of trying it, and because
they feel like they might fail

00:04:38.276 --> 00:04:40.364
they don't even do it, which is crazy.

00:04:40.364 --> 00:04:42.339
And then half the people may even do it

00:04:42.339 --> 00:04:44.435
and they try it once and then

00:04:44.435 --> 00:04:46.143
it doesn't work out so they fail.

00:04:46.143 --> 00:04:48.129
And then some people may
try it two or three times

00:04:48.129 --> 00:04:49.945
and it doesn't work and they quit.

00:04:49.945 --> 00:04:51.297
Would you be willing
to stick with something

00:04:51.297 --> 00:04:53.403
a thousand times, and keep testing

00:04:53.403 --> 00:04:55.461
and keep trying and keep improving?

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.294
Where most people would just

00:04:56.294 --> 00:04:57.671
see it as failure and they'll stop.

00:04:57.671 --> 00:04:59.726
And most people just quit too soon.

00:04:59.726 --> 00:05:02.885
And so just understand that
if you really want something,

00:05:02.885 --> 00:05:04.967
if you have a drive, a goal, an ambition

00:05:04.967 --> 00:05:07.926
to create something
that maybe is brand new,

00:05:07.926 --> 00:05:09.522
has never been done before,
or maybe you're following

00:05:09.522 --> 00:05:11.263
in someone else's footsteps
and has been done before.

00:05:11.263 --> 00:05:13.346
But if you really want to do something,

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.700
and you try it at the start
and it doesn't work out,

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.771
that's just step one in your journey.

00:05:17.771 --> 00:05:19.816
Don't stop on your path to doing

00:05:19.816 --> 00:05:21.535
something amazing that you want to do

00:05:21.535 --> 00:05:24.054
just because you didn't
have initial success.

00:05:24.054 --> 00:05:25.662
Most people quit way too soon.

00:05:25.662 --> 00:05:28.899
Most people quit before they're
going to hit the finish line.

00:05:28.899 --> 00:05:31.991
Where you could've had
a great, amazing career,

00:05:31.991 --> 00:05:35.331
but you stopped because you were afraid,

00:05:35.331 --> 00:05:37.398
and because you didn't
have initial success.

00:05:37.398 --> 00:05:40.857
A setback is not a
failure unless you quit.

00:05:40.857 --> 00:05:43.508
So the question of today is,
I'm curious, I want to know,

00:05:43.508 --> 00:05:46.450
When have you turned a setback into a win?

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.893
Talk to me about that process,

00:05:47.893 --> 00:05:49.505
talk to me about that experience,

00:05:49.505 --> 00:05:50.839
share down in the comments below

00:05:50.839 --> 00:05:52.432
and we'll join in the conversation.

00:05:52.432 --> 00:05:54.523
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Andrew Schultz.

00:05:54.523 --> 00:05:56.843
Andrew, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book.

00:05:56.843 --> 00:05:59.525
Your one word, it really really
really means a lot to me,

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:00.896
and I hope you're enjoying it.

00:06:00.896 --> 00:06:02.407
Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:06:02.407 --> 00:06:05.516
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:06:05.516 --> 00:06:07.359
and whatever your one word is,

00:06:07.359 --> 00:06:08.731
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:06:08.731 --> 00:06:11.104
for another shot of espresso.

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:13.589
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:13.589 --> 00:06:17.174
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:06:17.174 --> 00:06:19.469
Hey believe nation, thank
you so much for watching.

00:06:19.469 --> 00:06:21.662
If you want to learn
more about this subject,

00:06:21.662 --> 00:06:23.439
get a little bit deeper
on it, I'm going to share

00:06:23.439 --> 00:06:26.305
some extra bonus clips
that I hope you'll enjoy.

00:06:26.305 --> 00:06:29.413
- What has been the
best advice you received

00:06:29.413 --> 00:06:31.157
from your teacher or professor?

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:32.678
- Ooh I've gotten a lot of great advice

00:06:32.678 --> 00:06:35.078
from teacher, mentors,
professor throughout the years.

00:06:35.078 --> 00:06:39.820
So first of all, you got to
be open to taking some risks,

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:41.835
and not being afraid to fail.

00:06:41.835 --> 00:06:44.211
Failure is the key to success.

00:06:44.211 --> 00:06:45.546
So when you get to college,

00:06:45.546 --> 00:06:47.952
you got to raise your hand,
you have to be engaged.

00:06:47.952 --> 00:06:50.308
Don't be the kid thinking
"well I shouldn't be here,

00:06:50.308 --> 00:06:52.578
and maybe I'm not smart
enough, and maybe..."

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:57.035
No, you are more than
capable of going to college,

00:06:57.035 --> 00:06:58.763
being successful, and going on to do

00:06:58.763 --> 00:07:00.460
whatever you want in life.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.570
I sit here because I am you all.

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:05.997
There is no difference between me and you.

00:07:05.997 --> 00:07:09.399
Working class kid, growing up
on the South Side of Chicago,

00:07:09.399 --> 00:07:12.653
growing up with doubts and
fears just like all of you.

00:07:12.653 --> 00:07:14.713
I know exactly how you all are feeling,

00:07:14.713 --> 00:07:16.006
and kids out there who are thinking,

00:07:16.006 --> 00:07:17.849
maybe I'm not ready,
maybe I'm not good enough,

00:07:17.849 --> 00:07:19.601
maybe I can't afford it.

00:07:19.601 --> 00:07:21.581
But what teachers and mentors have told me

00:07:21.581 --> 00:07:24.313
is that yes you can, and you must.

00:07:24.313 --> 00:07:28.403
So get in there and be bold
with your intelligence.

00:07:28.403 --> 00:07:31.808
Raise your hand, get
support when you need it.

00:07:31.808 --> 00:07:36.321
And know that we all got here
because somebody helped us.

00:07:36.321 --> 00:07:37.915
- I listened to the people who were

00:07:37.915 --> 00:07:39.907
successful in selling that product.

00:07:39.907 --> 00:07:41.950
I would learn new things
from different ones,

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:46.507
new approaches, you must
be a constant student.

00:07:46.507 --> 00:07:48.901
A lot of people are
afraid to try anything new

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:52.173
because they are afraid of
that they will be embarrassed

00:07:52.173 --> 00:07:54.088
until they get good at it.

00:07:54.088 --> 00:07:56.891
Well on of my favorite sayings is,

00:07:56.891 --> 00:08:00.199
the most important thing you can do is to

00:08:00.199 --> 00:08:05.097
understand that anything worth
doing is worth doing poorly.

00:08:05.097 --> 00:08:06.160
- What do you mean by that?

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.559
- Until you can learn to do it well.

00:08:09.559 --> 00:08:12.485
My first few sales calls were pathetic,

00:08:12.485 --> 00:08:15.499
but I knew it was worth
doing so I kept after it.

00:08:15.499 --> 00:08:17.927
My first speeches were a disaster,

00:08:17.927 --> 00:08:21.028
but I believed that I
could develop into that,

00:08:21.028 --> 00:08:25.068
so I kept at it until I
could do it effectively.

00:08:25.068 --> 00:08:27.281
And all skills are exactly the same way.

00:08:27.281 --> 00:08:29.680
No running back that sets the records

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:32.909
every set a record the first
time he picked up a football.

00:08:32.909 --> 00:08:35.543
And you can go right
down the line with that.

00:08:35.543 --> 00:08:38.006
So if it's worth doing,
and you believe in it,

00:08:38.006 --> 00:08:40.740
go ahead and fail, and
the more times you fail,

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.310
the closer you're getting to
success because you should be

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:46.850
learning on every simple
thing that you do.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:48.474
- I am not here for me today,

00:08:48.474 --> 00:08:49.789
I'm here for every one of you all,

00:08:49.789 --> 00:08:52.393
because I kept going, because
I knew the day would come

00:08:52.393 --> 00:08:54.414
for one day I'd be standing
in front of a group of

00:08:54.414 --> 00:08:56.508
children and telling them
regardless of what happens

00:08:56.508 --> 00:08:58.412
to your life, regardless of the adversity,

00:08:58.412 --> 00:09:00.105
regardless of the
opposition, regardless of

00:09:00.105 --> 00:09:02.335
the trials and tribulations,
nothing can stop you.

00:09:02.335 --> 00:09:04.547
The only thing that can stop you is you.

00:09:04.547 --> 00:09:05.976
No situation, no circumstance,

00:09:05.976 --> 00:09:08.195
no piece of adversity
can define your life.

00:09:08.195 --> 00:09:10.028
Never let a circumstance define you.

00:09:10.028 --> 00:09:11.369
You see I knew something about you,

00:09:11.369 --> 00:09:12.945
I can speak from a certain place,

00:09:12.945 --> 00:09:15.661
I know something about you
without even knowing you.

00:09:15.661 --> 00:09:17.815
I know if you wanted to
come into this school,

00:09:17.815 --> 00:09:19.456
and do what you had to do, you can do it.

00:09:19.456 --> 00:09:21.267
I know if you wanted
to go into a classroom

00:09:21.267 --> 00:09:22.946
and get straight A's, you can do it.

00:09:22.946 --> 00:09:25.098
I know if you wanted to go
to college, you can do it.

00:09:25.098 --> 00:09:26.573
I know that you can become whatever

00:09:26.573 --> 00:09:27.842
it is that you want to become.

00:09:27.842 --> 00:09:29.152
But it's like that quote, you can lead

00:09:29.152 --> 00:09:31.633
a horse to water, but
you can't make him drink.

00:09:31.633 --> 00:09:33.127
You see, I could tell
you all the right things,

00:09:33.127 --> 00:09:34.934
I could stand up here
and say a presentation,

00:09:34.934 --> 00:09:36.692
but if you walk out of these doors,

00:09:36.692 --> 00:09:39.987
and you don't apply it to
your life, what good was it?

00:09:39.987 --> 00:09:42.748
You see I'm not so
concerned with you having

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:46.385
dreams, you having goals, I'm
concerned with the process.

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:48.522
Because a lot of people want the prize,

00:09:48.522 --> 00:09:51.216
but not many people want the process.

00:09:51.216 --> 00:09:53.257
A lot of people have the will to win,

00:09:53.257 --> 00:09:56.558
but few people have the
will to prepare to win.

00:09:56.558 --> 00:09:58.735
The process is more
important than the product.

00:09:58.735 --> 00:10:01.067
The process is more
important than the product.

00:10:01.067 --> 00:10:03.028
And what the process is,
the process is coming

00:10:03.028 --> 00:10:04.945
into this building day after day,

00:10:04.945 --> 00:10:06.976
giving everything you
got to mold yourself into

00:10:06.976 --> 00:10:08.991
the individual that you need to become

00:10:08.991 --> 00:10:10.755
in order to make those things happen.

00:10:10.755 --> 00:10:12.603
You know the reason you set goals?

00:10:12.603 --> 00:10:14.313
The reason you set goals and the reason

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:16.715
you have dreams is not for the outcome.

00:10:16.715 --> 00:10:20.283
The reason you have dreams
is to become the person

00:10:20.283 --> 00:10:21.701
that you need to become in order

00:10:21.701 --> 00:10:23.875
to make them manifest in your life.

00:10:23.875 --> 00:10:25.894
You see, young people, the road to success

00:10:25.894 --> 00:10:27.775
is constantly under construction.

00:10:27.775 --> 00:10:29.954
With plenty of potholes,
with plenty of speed bumps,

00:10:29.954 --> 00:10:30.985
with plenty of detours,

00:10:30.985 --> 00:10:33.028
with plenty of parking spots to give up.

00:10:33.028 --> 00:10:34.827
But just as if you were in
the car with your mother,

00:10:34.827 --> 00:10:36.381
you found a way to get
over that speed bump,

00:10:36.381 --> 00:10:38.116
you found a way to get
around that pothole,

00:10:38.116 --> 00:10:39.598
you found a way to get to that detour.

00:10:39.598 --> 00:10:42.358
The only thing about life, that
destination may be that goal

00:10:42.358 --> 00:10:43.535
or that dream or whatever it is that

00:10:43.535 --> 00:10:45.211
you aspire to do with your life.

00:10:45.211 --> 00:10:47.132
The one thing that I can
tell you right now man,

00:10:47.132 --> 00:10:49.322
I'm not anything special,
but the one thing I can

00:10:49.322 --> 00:10:50.577
guarantee you, young people,

00:10:50.577 --> 00:10:51.704
and I'm going to leave you with this.

00:10:51.704 --> 00:10:55.009
If you don't give, if you don't stop,

00:10:55.009 --> 00:10:57.969
if you don't give in,
nothing will defeat you,

00:10:57.969 --> 00:11:01.351
nothing will conquer you,
and nothing will stop you.

00:11:01.351 --> 00:11:05.480
Never give up, never stop,
never doubt yourself.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:07.559
You always believe there's always hope,

00:11:07.559 --> 00:11:09.580
and there's always somebody
inside you that's stronger

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.633
than anything that life can throw at you.

